This is a ROS2 humble workspace.
The language is Python or C++.
The ROS2 packages have been sourced.
The robot CPU is a jetson Orin Nano
This project is for the yahboomcar X3 robot with the S2 lidar and the Intel Realsense d435i camera.
Very important: Always check the terminal output for errors when running programs in the terminal.
There are two other workspaces that have relevent context:
    ~/yahboomcar_ros2/yahboom_X3_lib - contains the rosmaster library.
    ~/yahboomcar_ros2/library_ws - contains the lidar packages.
The client is on a separate machine (AMD64 Ubuntu 22.04) connected via ssh to the robot.
    A copy of the client code is at /home/mw/Robot_LLM
All test files should start with test_
Build ROS2 packages without --symlink-install
Important - The robot is a Jetson Orin Nano connected via ssh to a Ubuntu 22 PC.
All communications with the client are requested by the client (pull system)
Whenever possible, gracefully shut down your publisher node on the robot (e.g., Ctrl+C, not using kill -9)